## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```

